780:We proved that a $1$-saturated subcubic graph $G$ such that $g_3(G)=3$ is $(1,1,3,k)$-packing colorable for all $k\geq 3$. The result is sharp in the sense that there are such graphs that are not $(1,1,3)$-packing colorable (Proposition \ref{prop 2}) and there are such graphs that are not $(1,2,2)$-packing colorable (Proposition \ref{prop 3}).
