820:We proved that every $1$-saturated subcubic graph $G$ such that $g_3(G)\leq 4$ is $(1,2,2,2)$-packing colorable. The result is sharp in several senses: there are $1$-saturated subcubic graphs such that $g_3(G)\leq 4$ that are not $(1,2,2)$-packing colorable (Proposition \ref{prop 5}), there are $1$-saturated subcubic graphs such that $g_3(G)\geq 5$ that are not $(1,2,2,2)$-packing colorable (Proposition \ref{prop 6}), and there is a $2$-saturated subcubic graph $G$ such that $g_3(G)\leq 4$ that is not $(1,2,2,2)$-packing colorable (Proposition \ref{prop 7}).
