   762	
   763	We proved that a $0$-saturated subcubic graph $G$ such that $g_3(G)\leq 4$ admits both a  $(1,2,2,3)$-packing coloring and a $(2,2,2,2,3)$-packing coloring, except $\mathcal{G}_1$. Both results are sharp in the sense that there are such graphs that are not $(1,2,2)$-packing colorable and others that are not $(2,2,2,2)$-packing colorable (Proposition \ref{prop 1}).
