The paper already flags a critical Track-A issue: its proofs are constructive and explicitly “lead to efficient algorithms” for the guaranteed colorings. I’m reading the full proofs and sharpness section now to see whether there is still an honest Track B gap (large mechanical search versus a short structural insight), rather than rejecting merely because an algorithm exists.
