The module now builds two composable six-vertex tiles, randomizes their cyclic order and every vertex label, and independently recognizes the structure back from the edge set. Planted colorings and independently reconstructed colorings verify at all four presets; the six-vertex demo has 24 valid witnesses among 4,096 candidates. I’m running the full 200,000-sample gate and adversary panel now—the random-restart greedy attack is the likely failure point.
