/tmp/paper2603.0Jo5mw/main.tex:377:In this section, we prove three results. We start by a lemma about the structure of a $2$-saturated subcubic graph that will be a minimum counter example for the three results if they are supposed to be false. Then, we introduce two easy lemmas that will be useful in the coloring of the graphs in the main results.
