The Track B audit is decisive: the draft’s 155,520-operation “reference” cost comes from all-pairs BFS, but the paper’s proof never requires all-pairs distances here. Because the graph is subcubic and every relevant cycle has length at most four, each removable configuration is found by constant-radius inspection and the inductive coloring is linear. At the shipping graph’s 216 vertices and 252 edges, that is the same scale as the claimed 288-step “shortcut,” not a real compression gap. I’m quantifying that comparison and will record a formal H rejection rather than ship a misleading Track B claim.
