Rejected after full-text and measured Step 0 review.

The family passes G and V, but fails H:

- Track A: Section 2, Theorem 2 provides an efficient constructive coloring procedure for the promised regime.
- Track B: the optimized mechanical route is about 684 object visits, while the proposed shortcut already requires at least 468 input/output operations. There is no meaningful compression gap.
- The adversary panel also solved the draft frequently: local orientation 8/8, random greedy 5/8, visible-order greedy 1/8.

Deliverables:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.25113/REJECTED.md:1)
- [Retained generator draft](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.25113/rejected_gen_2603_25113.py:1)

The decision is based on the full [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.25113), not its abstract. Per the instructions, I stopped before the oracle loop rather than tuning attacks around a fundamentally easy family.
